---
import ProjectLayout from '../../layouts/ProjectLayout.astro';
import StannisCanvas from '../../components/StannisCanvas.astro';
---

<ProjectLayout slug="stannis">
  <StannisCanvas slot="scene" />

  <section>
    <h2>What it does</h2>
    <p class="lead">Stannis runs multi-step workflows on serverless Node.js. They survive restarts, scale across workers and resume from any point.</p>
    <p>
      Think AWS Step Functions, but as a plain JavaScript library you own and can run anywhere. State persists
      through a two-method storage adapter: Redis, DynamoDB, in-memory, or anything you wire up.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>The scene above</h2>
    <p>
      A live workflow. Each amber packet is a unit of work travelling through the graph: it splits into parallel
      sequences, merges, hits a decision, and in the race branch three competitors start and only the first to
      finish carries on.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Node types</h2>
    <div class="defs">
      <div class="def"><strong>Task</strong><span>A unit of work. Imports and runs an external module.</span></div>
      <div class="def"><strong>Sequence</strong><span>Runs child nodes one after another, in order.</span></div>
      <div class="def"><strong>Parallel</strong><span>Fans out to every branch and waits for all of them to finish.</span></div>
      <div class="def"><strong>Race</strong><span>Fans out to every branch. The first to finish wins; the rest are abandoned.</span></div>
      <div class="def"><strong>Decision</strong><span>Evaluates a condition and routes to exactly one branch.</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Key traits</h2>
    <ul class="list">
      <li>Durable across serverless cold starts and process restarts</li>
      <li>Storage-agnostic: bring your own adapter</li>
      <li>Resumable via continuation tokens, for human-in-the-loop flows</li>
      <li>Zero runtime dependencies. Plain JavaScript, typed with JSDoc</li>
      <li>Node.js 20+</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</ProjectLayout>
